## Gotchas
- Default first-boot login is `admin` / `admin` — change immediately.
- Organizer subfolders: overview always editable; preview cards list descendant notes (excluding world/campaign roots).
- Graph connections: PUT `/connections/:id` uses same visibility as POST; arrow direction is visual only for path highlight.
- AI session recaps use that session’s journal plus approved top-level glossary lines. Chronicle may dramatize; it must not invent off-journal facts. Recaps are editable by author/DM/admin without spending generation quota.
- Glossary exists only on World roots or standalone Campaigns (`is_glossary` stub note). Campaigns under a World use the World glossary. Search/mentions/AI corpus exclude glossary stubs.
- Do not commit one-off `RELEASE_NOTES*.md` / `release-*-notes.txt`; put release text in chat or GitHub Releases UI.
- `CONTEXT.md` is retired; this file is the only project context. `.cursor/` rules are versioned in git.
